# Show when guidance was reviewed

A review date says a person checked a piece of guidance. It is not a signal from Home Assistant and it cannot show that a device works.

These examples are local previews. Their dates are invented and do not record a real household inspection.

## Know which page owns what

[Page metadata and history](../components/page-history.html#child-civica-page-history-pattern) owns how dates are displayed. This pattern owns the decision to review and its scope. The [withdrawn review-date component](../components/review-date.html) stays for its existing route. No page generates a review date from a build.

## Review the whole page

Show review dates on guidance that depends on an integration, an interface or a household arrangement. Record the owner and what the review covered in the page source. Check the wording, links, supported controls and accessibility together before you change the last-reviewed date.

<%= example('nhs-pattern-review-guidance') %>

Do not add a review footer to a brightness dialog or a setup question. A live screen needs availability and request feedback. A review date there looks like freshness and misleads.

<%= example('nhs-review-distinct-times') %>

## Keep three kinds of date apart

- **Guidance reviewed:** a person checked all the instructions.
- **Content updated:** one part changed. Say what changed.
- **Reading received:** a device or integration reported a value at this time.

Give a real tutorial video its own review record. Review it when labels, navigation or device behaviour change, even if the page text does not. Do not extend its date during an unrelated build.

<%= example('nhs-review-overdue') %>

## Write the dates clearly

Use full dates and the `time` element. Give the time zone for readings where it matters. Place the dates at the end of the content they describe. Do not use a green “Current” badge on its own. People need to know what was checked and when. Leave an overdue date visible until someone really reviews the page.

## Respect Home Assistant behaviour

Record both the review and later edits in the page metadata. A deployment, an asset hash or a passing build is not a review. For live values, use the integration’s own timestamp and its documented freshness, not the time the page rendered. If there is no reliable observation time, say the time is unknown.

## Decide when to review

Choose an interval that fits the content and its owner. Review sooner after a Home Assistant change, a broken link or feedback. Archive or withdraw guidance nobody can maintain. Never reset its date to look current.
